DONE (2026-08-11):

1. [x] Performance Improvements
   - [x] suggestLinks no longer reads the whole links table. IDB v9 adds a
         compound [priority, added_at] index; explicit-priority rows come from
         it, null-priority rows (which IndexedDB cannot index — the reason
         this was parked) come from the existing added_at index, and the two
         cursor streams merge with early termination. The week page's own
         whole-library read went too: the search corpus now loads on first
         focus of the adder instead of on every page load.
         Tests: test/perfPaths.test.ts — ordering equivalence against the old
         implementation as oracle + a guard that fails if a whole-table
         getAll returns to the path.
   - [x] tagsByRecentUse no longer reads all link_tags. Recency lives in a
         LOCAL-ONLY label_usage store (one row per tag/topic id), stamped on
         assignment and rebuilt by a one-time backfill so existing ordering
         carried over. Deliberately NOT the synced last_used_at column the
         note suggested: stamping the tag row on every assignment would let a
         stale device clobber a concurrent rename under whole-row LWW — the
         exact stale-snapshot class the sync audit killed. Local-only gets
         the same 61k-to-120-row win with zero sync surface (and per-device
         recency is arguably the better UX). Docs: performance.md.
2. [x] Tracking-param stripping is configurable: user_settings gained
       strip_extra_params (SQLite v18 + sync.go + types + field-matrix).
       Settings → Link handling has an "Additional params to strip" textarea;
       entries are case-insensitive, trailing * matches a prefix. Applies to
       captures, the bulk re-strip, and whitelisted domains in 'all' mode.
3. [x] Auto-title apostrophe bug: real, and fixed in backend/title.go. The
       og:title regexes shared a [^"']+ class that stopped at EITHER quote
       character, so content="it doesn't matter your rank" captured
       "it doesn". Each quote style now matches to its own closing quote
       (RE2 has no backreferences); truncation is rune-safe; empty og:title
       falls through to <title>. Tests in title_test.go cover every
       quote/apostrophe combination.
4. [x] Cleanup
   - [x] Documentation overhaul: every doc in docs/dev (minus experiments &
         plans) and docs/user audited against the code by subagents and
         corrected — stale claims fixed (migration counters, sync triggers,
         wire format, week-close behavior, DSL grammar, seeder guarantees),
         missing coverage added (sync toggle, extra strip params, closed-week
         pruning, label_usage, resource-list capture).
   - [x] Code comments aligned across frontend and backend (stale headers,
         orphaned docstrings, dangling references to docs deleted in an old
         reorg, a literal NUL byte in topics.ts that made the file invisible
         to grep).
   - [x] Unused files removed: root package-lock.json (empty stub),
         frontend/public/favicon.svg (byte-identical duplicate of icon.svg),
         backend/backend.exe (stale build artifact), an empty next-tasks.md
         draft. Dead exports deleted (estimateLinks, storageEstimate,
         topicsByLinkMap, linksForTopic); five needlessly-exported internals
         un-exported. Test-only helpers deliberately kept.
   - [x] docs/dev/experiments & plans/further-cleanup.md written: a
         leverage-ordered refactor survey (reconcile-engine extraction,
         patch() completion, WeekApp/SettingsApp splits, DSL single source of
         truth, schema-triplication guard, doSync decomposition, and the
         known-limitation debt that is recorded but deliberately unbuilt).

Ensure for each change:

- if data model is updated
    - There are no sync issues/regressions with the changes
    - There are adequete tests for the system to ensure no synchronization issues, and that the system works both from the UI and has unit tests
    - Features that touch frontend and backend have testing and validation for both peices
- Add Changes to the CHANGELOG.md
    - If a version exists and does not have a release date yet, keep adding to it, if there's no versions without a release date, then bump version (e.g. `v0.1.0 -> v0.2.0`) in the version file, and add a new main heading to CHANGELOG.md for it (e.g. `v0.2.0 (unreleased)`) and add the changes under there.
    - Add all changes under the following categories as sub-headings:
      - Features
      - Bug Fixes
      - Other
        - For things like
          - Documentation improvements
          - Refinements to existing systems that weren't bugs
          - anything else that doesn't fit in the other sections
